{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1029466-is-it-feasible-to-hack-1st-ed-to-be-like-the-underworld-series","id":1029466,"title":"Is it feasible to hack 1st ed to be like the Underworld series?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-09T22:01:46-08:00","id":1029466,"title":"Is it feasible to hack 1st ed to be like the Underworld series?","content":"So I just watched Blood Wars tonight, and it reinvigorated my love for that series. And I got to thinking &quot;If I wanted an RPG of this, Requiem 1st ed might work&quot;. What is your opinion on the subject? Is it doable, a bad idea, or just kinda silly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T22:10:47-08:00","id":1029470,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen the new one (or any of them after 3, for that matter), but I would think CWoD would be your best bet for emulating Underworld, since it was originally a thinly disguised CWoD fan fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T22:12:25-08:00","id":1029472,"title":"","content":"Hm. I was mainly thinking the less substantial metaplot (and blood potency) could work, I'm curious, why do you think CWoD would work better? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T22:22:35-08:00","id":1029475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1029466-is-it-feasible-to-hack-1st-ed-to-be-like-the-underworld-series?p=1029470#post1029470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen the new one (or any of them after 3, for that matter), but I would think CWoD would be your best bet for emulating Underworld, since it was originally a thinly disguised CWoD fan fiction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know. Most of the things they &quot;borrowed&quot; from continued into Requiem - except the built in enmity with werewolves, but that's easy to add if you're borrowing setting elements from Underworld. If anything Requiem borrowed back (though not with the stealing a particular plotline from an earlier sold short story, so no copywrite issues) with the cyclical dynasties concept.<br /> <br /> I think the only thing VtM could give you that Requiem doesn't necessarily is Marcus's monstrous-man-bat form. But you wouldn't want to necessarily give him the rest of Vicissitude anyway, so you could probably hack together a Protean-based Elder Devotion to do it in Requiem.<br /> <br /> The big thing to add for vampires would be the relationship between memory and blood-consumption.<br /> <br /> For werewolves if you want to make them playable, Forsaken is better than Apocalypse, but it's still not a great fit because Underworld werewolves aren't spiritual entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T22:43:59-08:00","id":1029480,"title":"","content":"Hm. I'd probably have to write Lycans almost completely separate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T00:44:30-08:00","id":1029491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1029466-is-it-feasible-to-hack-1st-ed-to-be-like-the-underworld-series?p=1029475#post1029475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the only thing VtM could give you that Requiem doesn't necessarily is Marcus's monstrous-man-bat form. But you wouldn't want to necessarily give him the rest of Vicissitude anyway, so you could probably hack together a Protean-based Elder Devotion to do it in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't even need to try that hard. Protean 4 Unnatural Aspect. Wings are a viable option","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T07:21:41-08:00","id":1029586,"title":"","content":"Underworld was HEAVILY inspired by the first World of Darkness, if you want to play a game with the same theme your best bet is going classic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T07:35:37-08:00","id":1029591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MercSet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1029466-is-it-feasible-to-hack-1st-ed-to-be-like-the-underworld-series?p=1029491#post1029491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't even need to try that hard. Protean 4 Unnatural Aspect. Wings are a viable option</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not 1st ed though.<br /> <br /> I mean, 2nd would probably work just as well or even better, but the OP probably specified 1st for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T11:42:23-08:00","id":1029678,"title":"","content":"I specified 1st because 2nd is not a system I'm as familiar with, and that doesn't work as well with my preferred gaming medium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11866-thescottishfianna","name":"TheScottishFianna","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11866_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T14:25:05-08:00","id":1029756,"title":"","content":"I think the best argument for WoD over CofD is the system not the setting/themes.<br /> <br /> CofD combat (1e or 2e) is brutal. It's not a system that wants to do big cinematic fights, and it is hard to tune to that purpose. The WoD baseline combat system is much easier to do action movie fights in. It's still more lethal than you might want for Underworld, but you can much more easily create &quot;high level&quot; combatants that will get into big fights that will trade lots of blows and such, and &quot;low level&quot; combatants for them to mow down with ease.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:01:00-08:00","id":1029778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1029466-is-it-feasible-to-hack-1st-ed-to-be-like-the-underworld-series?p=1029475#post1029475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For werewolves if you want to make them playable, Forsaken is better than Apocalypse, but it's still not a great fit because Underworld werewolves aren't spiritual entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that it's fairly easy to hack Forsaken 2e into a form that's a reasonable fit for something like Underworld, unlike Forsaken 1e and Apocalypse. The way I'd do it would be to ditch the Uratha and focus instead on the Wolf-Blooded, with the Daughters of the Wolf having access to Wolf Gifts and the Sons of the Moon having access to Shadow Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:22:00-08:00","id":1029791,"title":"","content":"Do werewolves even have magic powers in Underworld? Seemed like they were just big brutes. You could have Uratha sans Gifts, just use senses and forms. Essence is gained by rest or eating people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:46:37-08:00","id":1029802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1029466-is-it-feasible-to-hack-1st-ed-to-be-like-the-underworld-series?p=1029791#post1029791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do werewolves even have magic powers in Underworld? Seemed like they were just big brutes. You could have Uratha sans Gifts, just use senses and forms. Essence is gained by rest or eating people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well most &quot;wolf gifts&quot; for Uratha generally are passable as just extreme versions of physical werewolf abilities, so including them is conceivable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:53:46-08:00","id":1029809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1029466-is-it-feasible-to-hack-1st-ed-to-be-like-the-underworld-series?p=1029802#post1029802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well most &quot;wolf gifts&quot; for Uratha generally are passable as just extreme versions of physical werewolf abilities, so including them is conceivable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess. Underworld werewolves didn't strike me as having that extreme of power. And you would still have to trim the wolf gifts of things like Lunacy affliction and giving Death Rage to your totem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T17:19:22-08:00","id":1029837,"title":"","content":"They're really more like the Cursed from the storyteller's guide, if you go with the option of them having a universal silver weakness. Just need to add in the capacity to induce the transformation without nearly killing themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T03:29:38-08:00","id":1029986,"title":"","content":"The Lycans are probably best modelled by mashing the werewolf and vampire templates together - shapeshifting, regeneration, silver, and senses from werewolves - disciplines, attribute-pumping, and integrity from vampires - they use vitae, but get it from human flesh rather than vampire blood - and they don't have a power stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T07:28:28-08:00","id":1030040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1029466-is-it-feasible-to-hack-1st-ed-to-be-like-the-underworld-series?p=1029986#post1029986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lycans are probably best modelled by mashing the werewolf and vampire templates together - shapeshifting, regeneration, silver, and senses from werewolves - disciplines, attribute-pumping, and integrity from vampires - they use vitae, but get it from human flesh rather than vampire blood - and they don't have a power stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>What purpose would that serve? Disciplines certainly cover a lot more than what werewolves can do. And I might just not be well versed in Underworld lore, but I don't think they need to eat human flesh period?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T07:43:59-08:00","id":1030051,"title":"","content":"Disciplines cover a lot more than what the <i>vampires</i> can do, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T08:29:14-08:00","id":1030067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1029466-is-it-feasible-to-hack-1st-ed-to-be-like-the-underworld-series?p=1030040#post1030040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What purpose would that serve? Disciplines certainly cover a lot more than what werewolves can do. And I might just not be well versed in Underworld lore, but I don't think they need to eat human flesh period?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if they <i>need</i> to, but there was a question in the first film, &quot;why would a werewolf be interested in a human except for food.&quot; Anyway, they probably should have to get their fuel from somewhere if vampires do, and the Forsaken mythos doesn't seem to suit Underworld at all. The other point of mashing like that is to drive home that the two species are siblings in this setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T08:49:35-08:00","id":1030077,"title":"","content":"I think there's a danger of this setting hack being of the &quot;to bits&quot; variety if we try to mimic the movies too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T09:52:10-08:00","id":1030099,"title":"","content":"Yeah basically if you're just going for straight Underworld, you don't need most of World of Darkness stuff. Healing, feeding, torpor, shapeshifting, vulnerability to silver and sunlight. You could do that with Dungeons and Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T10:47:32-08:00","id":1030130,"title":"","content":"You can always just use Dread Powers and Horrors to copy monsters that don't match a template. That might work better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}